# "Creatures your opponents control": Bot1's Nowhere to Run changes nothing about Bot1's own creatures. On turn four Bot2's
# Lightning Bolt cannot be aimed at Bot1's hexproof Sylvan Caryatid (the refusal, naming it) - the permission is for the
# creatures Bot1's opponents control, and Bot2's spells get none for Bot1's - while the same Bolt can be aimed at Bot1's Elvish
# Mystic (the positive control, which dies). Bot1's Nowhere to Run enters on turn three and kills Bot2's Elvish Mystic.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Sylvan Caryatid
Swamp
Elvish Mystic
Nowhere to Run
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Ruby
Elvish Mystic
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sylvan Caryatid.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Nowhere to Run.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
! Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Sylvan Caryatid)
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Elvish Mystic)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Elvish Mystic
Bot1.Graveyard = Elvish Mystic
Bot1.Battlefield.Sylvan Caryatid.Damage = 0
